abstract: >-
  Research software, three frozen English reports and computational/formal evidence
  for a deterministic two-player shared-pool Mahjong achievement game. Complete
  SAFE-state retrograde analysis and reverse replay classify the empty position
  as a second-player win. The October 2026 V17 run covers all 778,532,864,302 stored labels using
  natively compiled component checks. Whole-input assembly, exact coverage
  and cross-layer input identity retain external bookkeeping and custody
  assumptions under the generic kernel-proved implication. Native execution and external bookkeeping remain
  trusted; no closed actual-input opening Lean declaration or independent
  execution replication is claimed. A separate AI source/record review is supplied. Later fixed numerical/game
  proof pilots and same-host local-delivery tests are reported, with v2 repository corrections and supplementary retained records.
  Version and date identify the v2.0.0 research publication. This release
  adds privacy and evidence corrections; it does not claim a new game result
  or a closed opening Lean proof.
